# Covers: Tag.new() returns a tag that prints its name; a stop aimed at a
#         tag covering nothing is an ordinary call answering nil; freeze()
#         and unfreeze() are callable and answer nil.
#
# The outside-scope stop used to be a fatal ("tag.stop with no active
# scope").  The re-founded runtime retires that rule -- see
# tag_stop_no_target.chk for the reasoning and core design section 9 for
# the decision.  The stop-inside-its-own-scope half of the story is
# tests/chk/tag/scope_binds_user_tag.chk, which is where the tag register
# really does bind the scope.

var t = Tag.new("sc")
t.stop()
var t2 = Tag.new("fr")
t2.freeze()
t2.unfreeze()
[00000000] <Tag: sc>
[00000001] nil
[00000002] <Tag: fr>
[00000003] nil
[00000004] nil
